BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e646feba134c1d0a@ignite-gnv-events
DTSTAMP:20261001T174646Z
SUMMARY:Funding Innovation (workshop)
DTSTART:20260923T140000Z
DTEND:20260923T150000Z
LOCATION:UF Innovate | Sid Martin Biotech\, 12085 Research Dr.\, Alachua\, 
 FL 32615
URL:https://startgnv.com/event/funding-innovation-workshop/
DESCRIPTION:The session combines an educational seminar on SBIR/STTR and ot
 her federal funding opportunities with one-on-one office hours\, giving pa
 rticipants both a broad understanding of the programs and personalized gui
 dance tailored to their technology and funding goals.\nThe seminar provide
 s a practical overview of the U.S. non-dilutive funding ecosystem\, includ
 ing:\n• Introduction to SBIR/STTR and federal funding opportunities\n•
  Understanding the differences between agencies (NSF\, NIH\, DoD and other
 s)\n• Eligibility requirements and program structure\n• How to identif
 y the right agency for your technology\n• Proposal writing best practice
 s\n• Common pitfalls and how to avoid them\n• Funding strategy and com
 mercialization considerations\nParticipants will also have three 20-minute
  office hour time slots available after the seminar to discuss:\n• Techn
 ology fit for SBIR/STTR\n• Agency selection\n• Funding strategy\n• P
 roposal readiness\n• Next steps and commercialization pathway\nAfter reg
 istering for the event\, you’ll find the available time slots listed in 
 your confirmation email.About our speakers:Fernando Hernandez\nFernando He
 rnandez serves as the Vice President of Sales & Operations at Inspiralia U
 S\, where he leads business development and strategic partnerships. In thi
 s role\, he collaborates closely with startups\, universities\, incubators
 \, and innovation ecosystems to help organizations identify\, pursue\, and
  secure federal funding opportunities that support research\, innovation\,
  and growth.Berta Okenve\nBerta Okenve serves as the Head of Industry & He
 alth Projects at Inspiralia US\, where she specializes in helping innovati
 ve companies secure public funding for research and development. With expe
 rience supporting more than 100 U.S. and European organizations\, Berta ha
 s extensive expertise in Life Sciences\, Biotechnology\, Healthcare\, and 
 navigating funding opportunities through the National Institutes of Health
  (NIH)\, helping clients successfully access non-dilutive funding to advan
 ce their innovations.About our sponsor:Inspiralia\nInspiralia is an innova
 tion funding consultancy specializing in SBIR/STTR programs\, federal gran
 ts\, innovation funding strategy\, and commercialization support. The firm
  partners with startups\, universities\, and research organizations to ide
 ntify funding opportunities\, develop competitive grant proposals\, and ma
 nage the entire funding process—from opportunity identification through 
 award management.Thank you to our sponsor:———————UF Innovate
  | Accelerate\nUF Innovate | Accelerate is the University of Florida’s e
 ntrepreneurship support program that includes Sid Martin Biotech\, the glo
 bally recognized biotechnology incubator located in Progress Park in Alach
 ua\, Florida\, and The Hub\, the globally recognized diversified tech incu
 bator located in Gainesville’s Innovation District.\nHosted by: CIED | S
 anta Fe College\nstartGNV: https://startgnv.com/event/funding-innovation-w
 orkshop/
END:VEVENT
