BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:33f04de8611eec2e@ignite-gnv-events
DTSTAMP:20261001T174646Z
SUMMARY:From Bench To Automation (Lunch & Learn)
DTSTART:20261105T160000Z
DTEND:20261105T183000Z
LOCATION:UF Innovate | Sid Martin Biotech\, 12085 Research Dr.\, Alachua\, 
 FL 32615
URL:https://calendar.ufl.edu/innovate/event/57594-from-bench-to-automation-
 lunch-learn
DESCRIPTION:From 11 AM – 1 PM in the Sid Martin main lobby\, attendees ar
 e invited to stop by for lunch\, refreshments\, and conversation with our 
 laboratory automation specialists. Rather than focusing on a single applic
 ation or product\, the session is designed around the work being done by c
 ompanies within the Sid Martin community.\nBring us your workflow. Whether
  you are working with PCR and qPCR\, NGS\, genomics\, cell-based assays\, 
 sample preparation\, assay development\, plate-based workflows\, reagent d
 ispensing\, normalization\, dilution series\, or another application\, we 
 can discuss how automation could potentially fit into your process.\nThe g
 oal is to help answer questions such as:\n– What parts of my current wor
 kflow can realistically be automated?\n– When does automation make sense
  and when does it not?\n– How can automation improve reproducibility and
  consistency?\n– Can automation help reduce hands-on time or increase th
 roughput?\n– How do you translate an existing manual protocol into an au
 tomated workflow?\n– What should a lab consider before implementing liqu
 id handling automation?\nAn Eppendorf automated liquid handling platform w
 ill be available so attendees can see the technology and discuss specific 
 applications with the team.\nFollowing the Lunch & Learn\, from approximat
 ely 1 – 1:30 PM\, Eppendorf will host a more focused 20-30 minute educat
 ional presentation in the conference room covering the fundamentals of lab
 oratory automation\, common applications\, workflow development\, and cons
 iderations when transitioning from manual pipetting to automated liquid ha
 ndling. Meet with Phillip Tender and Taylor Smith of Eppendorf.\nTerrie Gu
 nter of USA Scientific will also be onsite during the event to meet with a
 ttendees and support discussions around laboratory workflows\, consumables
 \, and automation applications.About our speakers:Philip Tendler\nPhilip T
 endler supports laboratory automation and floor model centrifugation techn
 ologies throughout the Southeastern United States for Eppendorf North Amer
 ica. With a graduate background in molecular genetics from the University 
 of Georgia and experience working with academic\, biotechnology\, pharmace
 utical\, and research laboratories\, Philip focuses on helping scientists 
 evaluate technologies that can improve workflow efficiency\, reproducibili
 ty\, throughput\, and overall laboratory productivity.Taylor Smith\nTaylor
  Smith is an Application Integration Specialist with Eppendorf North Ameri
 ca\, specializing in automated liquid handling applications and workflow d
 evelopment. Taylor works directly with scientists to understand existing l
 aboratory protocols\, identify opportunities for automation\, and translat
 e manual processes into reliable automated workflows. During the event\, T
 aylor will be available to discuss individual applications and the practic
 al considerations involved in developing automated methods. Thank you to o
 ur sponsors:\n\n ———————UF Innovate | Accelerate\nUF Innovat
 e | Accelerate is the University of Florida’s entrepreneurship support p
 rogram that includes Sid Martin Biotech\, the globally recognized biotechn
 ology incubator located in Progress Park in Alachua\, Florida\, and The Hu
 b\, the globally recognized diversified tech incubator located in Gainesvi
 lle’s Innovation District.\nHosted by: UF Innovate\nstartGNV: https://st
 artgnv.com/event/from-bench-to-automation-lunch-learn/\nUF Innovate: https
 ://calendar.ufl.edu/innovate/event/57594-from-bench-to-automation-lunch-le
 arn
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:df16aac6436e2957@ignite-gnv-events
DTSTAMP:20261001T174646Z
SUMMARY:From Frat House To Franchising (Seminar)
DTSTART:20261105T190000Z
DTEND:20261105T200000Z
LOCATION:UF Innovate | The Hub\, 747 SW Second Avenue\, Gainesville\, FL 32
 607
URL:https://calendar.ufl.edu/innovate/event/58247-from-frat-house-to-franch
 ising-seminar
DESCRIPTION:Join Matt Friedman at UF Innovate | The Hub as he shares the st
 ory of turning a $500 investment and a fraternity-house kitchen in Gainesv
 ille into the global WING ZONE franchise.\n\n Please register by noon on N
 ovember 4th.\nHosted by: UF Innovate\nUF Innovate: https://calendar.ufl.ed
 u/innovate/event/58247-from-frat-house-to-franchising-seminar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7c6132ad9435028f@ignite-gnv-events
DTSTAMP:20261001T174646Z
SUMMARY:celebrateGNV 2026
DTSTART:20261105T230000Z
DTEND:20261106T020000Z
LOCATION:Cade Museum for Creativity and Invention\, 811 S Main Street\, Gai
 nesville\, FL 32601
URL:https://startgnv.com/event/celebrategnv-2026/
DESCRIPTION:The premier annual celebration of North Central Florida's thriv
 ing innovation ecosystem\, organized by startGNV.\n\ncelebrateGNV: Honorin
 g Innovation in North Central Florida\n\nJoin us for an evening of celebra
 tion of the individuals and companies that are driving North Central Flori
 da’s thriving startup and innovation ecosystem. celebrateGNV brings toge
 ther entrepreneurs\, mentors\, business leaders\, and community builders f
 or an inspiring dinner event recognizing those who are making a real diffe
 rence in our region.\n\nWhat to Expect\n\n• Dinner experience with wine 
 and beer service\n\n• Award presentations honoring outstanding contribut
 ors to our innovation community\n\n• Networking opportunities with fello
 w entrepreneurs\, mentors\, and business leaders\n\n• Inspiring stories 
 from those building the future of North Central Florida’s startup scene\
 n\nAwards Categories\n\n• Professional Mentor of the Year – Recognizin
 g exceptional guidance and support\n\n• Community Builder – Celebratin
 g those who strengthen our entrepreneurial ecosystem\n\n• Employer of th
 e Year – Honoring companies creating opportunities and fostering innovat
 ion\n\n• Community Impact Company of the Year – Recognizing establishe
 d companies making a meaningful difference in our region\n\n• Rising Sta
 r Startup – Celebrating a pre-seed startup with exceptional potential fo
 r success (includes $5\,000 prize)\n\nWhether you’re a startup founder\,
  seasoned entrepreneur\, mentor\, or simply passionate about innovation in
  North Central Florida\, this is your opportunity to celebrate achievement
 s\, connect with like-minded professionals\, and be inspired by the incred
 ible work happening in our community.\n\nCome raise a glass to the people 
 and organizations making North Central Florida a premier destination for s
 tartups and innovation!\nHosted by: startGNV\nstartGNV: https://startgnv.c
 om/event/celebrategnv-2026/\nstartGNV (Eventbrite): https://www.eventbrite
 .com/e/celebrategnv-2026-tickets-1743805381839
END:VEVENT
